WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:25.063 --> 00:00:29.230
(ethereal music)
(water churns softly)

00:01:07.535 --> 00:01:12.079
(hair brushes)
(toothbrush brushes)

00:01:12.079 --> 00:01:15.250
(water runs)

00:01:15.250 --> 00:01:17.750
(pan sizzles)

00:01:20.420 --> 00:01:23.553
- My name is Sonja Hyppanen,
and I'm born in Finland

00:01:23.553 --> 00:01:27.262
and I've been with Sea
Shepard for five years now.

00:01:27.262 --> 00:01:30.082
My training from uni is journalism.

00:01:30.082 --> 00:01:32.415
I still go back to that job.

00:01:34.994 --> 00:01:36.976
- [Woman] By far most of the
people within Sea Shepard

00:01:36.976 --> 00:01:39.441
are volunteers even if this is a massive,

00:01:39.441 --> 00:01:43.265
global organization, it's not so much like

00:01:43.265 --> 00:01:45.414
I'm in the military or whatever.

00:01:45.414 --> 00:01:48.028
I just protect what's closest to my heart.

00:01:48.028 --> 00:01:51.604
(soft piano music)

00:01:51.604 --> 00:01:53.886
- [Man] The open ocean is a lawless area.

00:01:53.886 --> 00:01:57.666
The UN is just starting
to address that now.

00:01:57.666 --> 00:01:59.244
- [Man] There's not
many organizations left

00:01:59.244 --> 00:02:02.927
that do what they do and
go thousands of miles,

00:02:02.927 --> 00:02:05.541
you know, trying to protect the
marine life in the waters.

00:02:05.541 --> 00:02:08.458
(soft piano music)

00:02:12.893 --> 00:02:14.503
- [Man] Just like the
strength of an ecosystem

00:02:14.503 --> 00:02:16.504
is in diversity, the
strength of any movement

00:02:16.504 --> 00:02:17.737
lies in diversity.

00:02:17.737 --> 00:02:21.570
So this is why we're a
volunteer organization.

00:02:22.980 --> 00:02:25.079
- [Man] And I think
okay we say we come here

00:02:25.079 --> 00:02:27.153
with a motivation, it's
beyond motivation and to be

00:02:27.153 --> 00:02:29.461
committed to something that's right.

00:02:29.461 --> 00:02:32.446
(people chatter)
(soft music)

00:02:32.446 --> 00:02:33.905
- [Man] If you look on
the earth as a spaceship,

00:02:33.905 --> 00:02:37.193
which is what it is, we're
traveling around the galaxy,

00:02:37.193 --> 00:02:39.011
every spaceship has a life support system

00:02:39.011 --> 00:02:41.875
and our life support system
is that biodiversity,

00:02:41.875 --> 00:02:43.365
especially in the ocean.

00:02:43.365 --> 00:02:46.115
(ethereal music)

00:02:49.429 --> 00:02:50.480
- [Man] The land is small.

00:02:50.480 --> 00:02:52.768
You know, it’s 30-percent of this whole
planet and that's what

00:02:52.768 --> 00:02:54.273
we think of, "Oh the land."

00:02:54.273 --> 00:02:58.781
You know, but the ocean, really
the planet is the ocean.

00:02:58.781 --> 00:03:00.258
- [Man] The ocean provides
us everything

00:03:00.258 --> 00:03:01.754
that we need to survive.

00:03:01.754 --> 00:03:03.495
It produces oxygen, it produces food,

00:03:03.495 --> 00:03:05.561
regulates climate and temperature.

00:03:05.561 --> 00:03:08.311
(ethereal music)

00:03:19.347 --> 00:03:22.496
- [Man] Well it gets back
to that essential mantra

00:03:22.496 --> 00:03:25.240
that if the oceans die, we die.

00:03:25.240 --> 00:03:28.157
(harpoon explodes)

00:03:29.066 --> 00:03:32.233
But the power of money and consumption

00:03:33.572 --> 00:03:36.169
has been overriding all of that.

00:03:36.169 --> 00:03:37.373
- [Man] They've always said that they're

00:03:37.373 --> 00:03:39.219
conducting scientific research.

00:03:39.219 --> 00:03:41.454
So the International Code
of Justice underlined that.

00:03:41.454 --> 00:03:43.063
They basically said that
what whalers are doing

00:03:43.063 --> 00:03:46.142
is in fact a poaching operation.

00:03:46.142 --> 00:03:48.809
(radio mumbles)

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:56.105
- [Man] There's not
these surpluses of stuff

00:03:56.105 --> 00:03:58.340
lying around in the ocean, it's all there

00:03:58.340 --> 00:04:01.440
in the amount that it needs
to be for the ocean to live.

00:04:01.440 --> 00:04:03.108
(gulls cry)

00:04:03.108 --> 00:04:05.608
(clocks tick)

00:04:06.795 --> 00:04:09.378
- [Man] So Sea Shepard
steps in in accordance

00:04:09.378 --> 00:04:12.036
with the United Nations
World Charter for Nature.

00:04:12.036 --> 00:04:13.992
- [Man] So we enforce the
International Conservation Law

00:04:13.992 --> 00:04:16.791
against illegal fishing (mumbles).

00:04:16.791 --> 00:04:21.181
- [Radio] Yeah I've got a
radar target hit about nine miles.

00:04:21.181 --> 00:04:22.567
- [Radio] Did you see
anything over that way?

00:04:22.567 --> 00:04:25.175
(radio mumbles)

00:04:25.175 --> 00:04:27.422
It definitely looks
like a ship on the radar

00:04:27.422 --> 00:04:30.363
so it looks like about 11 o'clock.

00:04:30.363 --> 00:04:32.789
(radio mumbles)
(bell rings)

00:04:32.789 --> 00:04:34.516
- [Radio] Dispel crew, dispel crew.

00:04:34.516 --> 00:04:37.574
Close all dampers, close all dampers.

00:04:37.574 --> 00:04:39.913
Meet at station, meet at station.

00:04:39.913 --> 00:04:42.299
(bell rings)
(suspenseful music)

00:04:42.299 --> 00:04:44.673
- [Man] It's not just a
protest, it's not just

00:04:44.673 --> 00:04:47.303
banner waving or petition signing,

00:04:47.303 --> 00:04:49.638
it's getting physically involved

00:04:49.638 --> 00:04:51.160
and making a difference.

00:04:51.160 --> 00:04:53.984
- [Radio] You can bring
in the defensive lines.

00:04:53.984 --> 00:04:55.695
(mumbles) in the water.

00:04:55.695 --> 00:04:57.642
(suspenseful music)

00:04:57.642 --> 00:05:00.481
- [Man] Do you have all
the lines nice and tight?

00:05:00.481 --> 00:05:01.836
(mumbles)

00:05:01.836 --> 00:05:03.831
We are going in the water.

00:05:03.831 --> 00:05:07.149
- [Man] It's challenging
the system and the system

00:05:07.149 --> 00:05:09.247
is in favor of the bureaucracy.

00:05:09.247 --> 00:05:11.039
- They are ready to deploy.

00:05:11.039 --> 00:05:12.456
- [Man] And when you try
and stand up against that,

00:05:12.456 --> 00:05:14.536
it's odd the reaction you get.

00:05:14.536 --> 00:05:15.619
- [Man] Try and go and close it.

00:05:15.619 --> 00:05:17.449
Make a (mumbles).

00:05:17.449 --> 00:05:20.616
(radio mumble orders)

00:05:25.818 --> 00:05:26.651
- [Man On Loud Speaker] You are whaling

00:05:26.651 --> 00:05:28.394
illegally in these waters.

00:05:28.394 --> 00:05:29.378
You have been condemned by the

00:05:29.378 --> 00:05:31.171
International Code of Justice.

00:05:31.171 --> 00:05:33.921
(dramatic music)

00:05:35.153 --> 00:05:36.130
- [Man] To be honest, if we
were doing the wrong thing,

00:05:36.130 --> 00:05:37.436
the Sea Shepard would be shut down.

00:05:37.436 --> 00:05:39.591
I wouldn't be able to volunteer.

00:05:39.591 --> 00:05:40.963
- [Man On Loud Speaker] Your
acts are not in accordance

00:05:40.963 --> 00:05:43.203
with the international rules of the road.

00:05:43.203 --> 00:05:46.340
What you are doing is illegal,
we are doing nothing wrong.

00:05:46.340 --> 00:05:47.509
You're crossing our port side,

00:05:47.509 --> 00:05:48.780
you're crossing our port side.

00:05:48.780 --> 00:05:50.257
You must give way.

00:05:50.257 --> 00:05:52.444
- [Radio] Please brace for
collision, brace for collision.

00:05:52.444 --> 00:05:56.067
(radio mumbles frantically)
(boats crash)

00:05:56.067 --> 00:05:57.760
- [Woman] Stop, stop.

00:05:57.760 --> 00:06:00.654
(gun fires)

00:06:00.654 --> 00:06:03.321
(water sprays.)

00:06:04.704 --> 00:06:05.537
- [Man On Loud Speaker] You have purposely

00:06:05.537 --> 00:06:07.190
endangered our crew
and damaged our vessel.

00:06:07.190 --> 00:06:11.436
Change your course to port
to prevent further damage.

00:06:11.436 --> 00:06:13.924
(people yell excitedly)

00:06:13.924 --> 00:06:16.192
- [Radio] The whole fishing
vessel aside your starboard.

00:06:16.192 --> 00:06:17.025
- [Man On Loud Speaker] You're fishing

00:06:17.025 --> 00:06:18.101
illegally in these waters.

00:06:18.101 --> 00:06:19.790
- [Man] People just came up and were like,

00:06:19.790 --> 00:06:20.674
"What are you guys?

00:06:20.674 --> 00:06:22.549
"What is what you're doing?"

00:06:22.549 --> 00:06:24.334
And just couldn't figure it out at all

00:06:24.334 --> 00:06:27.752
with the jolly and the
logos and everyone in black.

00:06:27.752 --> 00:06:30.279
- [Woman] We only go
against illegal operators

00:06:30.279 --> 00:06:33.087
so with authorities, we
do everything by the book.

00:06:33.087 --> 00:06:35.394
It's very important
for us to be recognized

00:06:35.394 --> 00:06:38.561
as a legitimate law enforcement force.

00:06:41.774 --> 00:06:43.308
- [Man] Many of them have
never been to sea before.

00:06:43.308 --> 00:06:47.475
Many of them have never done
anything like this before.

00:06:54.107 --> 00:06:57.560
- [Woman] The ocean is not
very well at the moment.

00:06:57.560 --> 00:07:01.023
It's pretty sick and needs a lot of help.

00:07:01.023 --> 00:07:04.106
(sad ethereal music)

00:07:11.009 --> 00:07:12.074
- [Man] So really what we're talking about

00:07:12.074 --> 00:07:15.991
is a movement to save
ourselves from ourselves.

00:07:18.183 --> 00:07:19.016
- [Man] Everybody doing okay?

00:07:19.016 --> 00:07:20.544
Anybody want to go get some rest?

00:07:20.544 --> 00:07:22.961
(soft music)

00:07:24.878 --> 00:07:27.824
- [Woman] We have people who
are 18, people who are 65.

00:07:27.824 --> 00:07:30.431
They're artists, they're
lawyers, they're plumbers,

00:07:30.431 --> 00:07:33.921
journalists, different
religious backgrounds.

00:07:33.921 --> 00:07:36.487
You know, I’m just a normal girl from a little town.

00:07:36.487 --> 00:07:38.904
(soft music)

00:07:41.044 --> 00:07:43.474
How I perceive the world,
everything's connected.

00:07:43.474 --> 00:07:45.349
Your oceans are connected to the land

00:07:45.349 --> 00:07:46.559
which is connected to the people

00:07:46.559 --> 00:07:48.377
so if we keep depleting the fish stocks

00:07:48.377 --> 00:07:50.567
with overfishing, illegal fishing,

00:07:50.567 --> 00:07:53.547
there's no food for people on the planet.

00:07:53.547 --> 00:07:55.237
(train rumbles)

00:07:55.237 --> 00:07:56.763
I do believe every human being is

00:07:56.763 --> 00:07:58.330
good at their hearts, so

00:07:58.330 --> 00:08:01.221
if you give them the correct
information they will change.

00:08:01.221 --> 00:08:03.952
And I think it's something
I've been looking for

00:08:03.952 --> 00:08:05.509
the whole of my life, how I can make a

00:08:05.509 --> 00:08:08.834
direct impact for the
well-being of the planet.

00:08:08.834 --> 00:08:12.334
(string orchestral music)

00:08:21.620 --> 00:08:23.281
- [Man] Come along you!

00:08:23.281 --> 00:08:24.114
Oh, here it is!

00:08:24.114 --> 00:08:24.947
Here it is!

00:08:24.947 --> 00:08:26.494
Wooo!

00:08:26.494 --> 00:08:30.661
(string orchestral ethereal music)

00:08:39.980 --> 00:08:41.859
- [Man] Sea Shepard can't
spend the next 50 years

00:08:41.859 --> 00:08:44.624
in the Antarctic policing
the anti-whaling campaign,

00:08:44.624 --> 00:08:46.022
but also the governments can't afford it,

00:08:46.022 --> 00:08:47.317
so we have to educate the people that

00:08:47.317 --> 00:08:48.805
it's not the right thing to do

00:08:48.805 --> 00:08:51.138
and that is the way forward.

00:08:52.489 --> 00:08:55.127
- [Man] There's almost
a key moment to join

00:08:55.127 --> 00:08:58.590
any sort of fight that is
gonna try to bring a change.

00:08:58.590 --> 00:09:02.411
Everything counts in this
very moment of history.

00:09:02.411 --> 00:09:03.742
- [Man] We're not here to be pessimistic

00:09:03.742 --> 00:09:05.733
'cause we know we've
got something to save.

00:09:05.733 --> 00:09:10.366
If there's nothing to
save we wouldn't be here.

00:09:10.366 --> 00:09:11.260
- [Man] It's not like you get

00:09:11.260 --> 00:09:12.482
another chance at these things.

00:09:12.482 --> 00:09:15.416
You know, once it's gone, it's
very often, that's it.

00:09:15.416 --> 00:09:18.166
(ethereal music)

00:09:37.890 --> 00:09:40.390
(piano music)

00:09:48.610 --> 00:09:49.888
- We don't try to say that Sea Shepard's

00:09:49.888 --> 00:09:51.477
gonna save the world

00:09:51.477 --> 00:09:52.310
We're not.

00:09:52.310 --> 00:09:54.332
But we can set an example for others.

00:09:54.332 --> 00:09:55.886
- Met a lot of really
great passionate people

00:09:55.886 --> 00:09:58.028
and it's nice to just be part of something

00:09:58.028 --> 00:10:00.145
where people haven't given up hope.

00:10:00.145 --> 00:10:02.074
- It's not a point where we can't move

00:10:02.074 --> 00:10:03.583
forward positively, absolutely not.

00:10:03.583 --> 00:10:04.868
And I think the fight is a good one

00:10:04.868 --> 00:10:07.104
and it's just education.

00:10:07.104 --> 00:10:09.604
(piano music)

00:10:17.105 --> 00:10:18.944
- When people get to
know about Sea Shepard,

00:10:18.944 --> 00:10:20.981
it's mostly you know them from TV,

00:10:20.981 --> 00:10:22.383
you know the direct actions.

00:10:22.383 --> 00:10:24.111
- The media can transport
quite a different

00:10:24.111 --> 00:10:26.907
image of what this organization is about

00:10:26.907 --> 00:10:28.487
and what we actually do.

00:10:28.487 --> 00:10:30.398
- People know us from the
anti-whaling campaigns

00:10:30.398 --> 00:10:33.755
in the Antarctic, but of
course, we've done a lot more.

00:10:33.755 --> 00:10:36.415
- I'll walk into a room
and they'll look at me

00:10:36.415 --> 00:10:40.829
and they'll go, "Wow, we didn't
think you'd look like that."

00:10:40.829 --> 00:10:43.329
(piano music)

00:10:56.443 --> 00:10:58.839
- You have to work with
so many different people

00:10:58.839 --> 00:11:00.135
depending on their background,

00:11:00.135 --> 00:11:02.989
depending on their education or their

00:11:02.989 --> 00:11:05.457
religion, their culture.

00:11:05.457 --> 00:11:07.453
- They're as good as any professional crew

00:11:07.453 --> 00:11:11.222
I've ever witnessed because
they want to be there.

00:11:11.222 --> 00:11:13.095
They're not just in it for the money.

00:11:13.095 --> 00:11:14.772
- This is exactly the reason why

00:11:14.772 --> 00:11:18.248
I wanted to join Sea Shepard using

00:11:18.248 --> 00:11:20.676
direct action and not just witnessing

00:11:20.676 --> 00:11:22.719
illegal activities happening or injustice

00:11:22.719 --> 00:11:25.106
happening in our oceans.

00:11:25.106 --> 00:11:27.053
- And that's what I
think makes us so strong

00:11:27.053 --> 00:11:29.720
that we can make the
bond between everybody

00:11:29.720 --> 00:11:32.410
and then work together when there are

00:11:32.410 --> 00:11:34.807
situations that we need to do actions in.

00:11:34.807 --> 00:11:37.307
(piano music)

00:12:04.675 --> 00:12:06.696
- I think it's interesting
how they always say it's

00:12:06.696 --> 00:12:08.896
eco-terrorists and pirates
and all these different things

00:12:08.896 --> 00:12:11.844
and yet I turn in my sea
time to the U.S. Coast Guard.

00:12:11.844 --> 00:12:13.720
At every port I have to
clear in with the Police

00:12:13.720 --> 00:12:15.533
so I'm never arrested.

00:12:15.533 --> 00:12:19.619
- The Sea Shepard are, you know, pirates
and they stand up against.

00:12:19.619 --> 00:12:21.284
You go, "Well, that's one opinion.

00:12:21.284 --> 00:12:24.496
“And every issue has two sides to it."

00:12:24.496 --> 00:12:28.413
- I meet a lot of young
people who see through this

00:12:28.413 --> 00:12:30.478
and they are the ones who I think will be

00:12:30.478 --> 00:12:31.528
starting to change.

00:12:31.528 --> 00:12:33.516
- The movement doesn't have any leaders.

00:12:33.516 --> 00:12:34.355
When I look around the world,

00:12:34.355 --> 00:12:36.688
all the great social achievements

00:12:36.688 --> 00:12:38.059
have been done by individuals.

00:12:38.059 --> 00:12:41.039
- Well it brings together
people from all walks of life.

00:12:41.039 --> 00:12:44.144
- Older people, younger people.

00:12:44.144 --> 00:12:45.149
Uh, you know, some crazy people.

00:12:45.149 --> 00:12:47.378
(laughs)

00:12:47.378 --> 00:12:51.545
But, yeah, just, you know, people like you and me
in a day to day, whatever.

00:12:52.548 --> 00:12:55.048
(piano music)

